        The driver was releasing the reference count of i_private data (e.g., aa_loaddata) when removing the dentry from the filesystem, but the inode can persist and be accessed via open file descriptors after that point. This creates a race condition where the data is freed before the filesystem callbacks finish using it, leading to use-after-free.

